  "interpretation": [
    "Productive_walk performs only62 observed evacuation moves in44/636 games, versus7400 observed in-range camp retargets in312games. Evacuation addresses a narrow capture handoff opportunity, not most camp farming.",
    "Walking banking is frequently called; its pooled fallback counter is a small fraction of sampled decisions but appears in roughly half of games. Risk mode attempts its safe-mask executor on most sampled banking decisions. An executor not moving is not itself proof it blocked a dangerous step.",
    "Optional recall filtering is frequent (about62% of sampled productive_walk opportunities). cr_started also includes ordinary successful capture recalls, while cr_opportunity counts only evaluated optional predicates (short-circuited when normal want_recall is true), so their ratio is not an acceptance rate.",
    "Tavi-specific skip counters remain zero in these samples; that does not establish no Tavi drafts or no possible usefulness. Path-unavailable36 observations appear in12games, not a demonstrated frequent routing failure.",
    "Productive_walk preserves/slightly raises work rates and slightly lowers death rate against matched baseline, but the matched panel remains negative. Delivery ratio barely changes; neither tiny native deltas nor positive direct self-play establish broader strength.",
    "The focus component is absent. These packages address camp target reach, reward handoff, walking/risk-aware banking and optional return cost; they do not constitute a comprehensive new contested-camp combat policy."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Counter maxima and positive-game counts are sampled lower bounds. Fractions formed from two lower-bound counter sums are descriptive ratios of observed maxima, not bounds on the true event fraction.",
    "Evacuation requires a healthy nonchanneling ally already on the reward, an alternate target and a legal safe improving exit. Rare observed activation is expected from those narrow prerequisites; missing samples can hide trailing activations.",
    "br_routes counts attempts using the risk mask, not guaranteed movement or safety; ordinary walk mode intentionally records zero. Fallback reasons (fuel/query/unreachable/all-unsafe) are pooled and cannot be separated with these counters.",
    "Native rate changes are paired descriptive endpoints over complete games, not controlled attribution to one feature. Team size, match duration, opponents and interaction effects can influence them.",
    "cf_reward_gain_observed and death-after-recent-camp are proxies, not exact unique capture counts or causal death attribution. Baseline lacks these new policy counters.",
    "Adaptive development screen53, five fixed references and reused physical keys do not substitute for frozen fresh confirmation or online-ladder validation."
  ],
